course: dictionary
lesson: 6454
title: Names with a capital letter
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A proper name is the name of one special person, place or thing, and it always starts with a capital letter. «Nara» is the name of a city in Japan, so it has a capital N. A dictionary often marks it as a name.
explain: The same letters can mean something different. «The nara is also a spiky melon plant» in the deserts of Namibia. Here nara has no capital letter, so it is an ordinary word for a plant. The capital letter tells you it is a name.
explain: Some words are short for longer names. NARA stands for the National Archives and Records Administration of the USA, which keeps important government papers. When all the letters are capitals, look for a long name hidden inside.
fact: A proper name starts with a capital letter, even in the middle of a sentence.
fact: «Nara» is a city in Japan that was once its capital.
fact: Nara is famous for its old temples and for the tame deer that walk freely in Nara Park.
fact: «About 1,200 sika deer roam freely in Nara, Japan, as protected sacred animals.»
fact: The deer have learned to bob their heads for special crackers, but they sometimes butt people who tease them.
exercise: «About 1,200 sika deer roam freely in Nara, Japan.» Where do the deer roam? | *In Nara, Japan | In a zoo in Namibia | In the USA, in a government building
exercise: What does the word NARA stand for in the USA? | A spiky melon plant | A city in Japan | *The National Archives and Records Administration | Nara Park
exercise: «The nara is a spiky melon plant that grows in the deserts of Namibia.» Why does nara have no capital letter here? | Because it is a sentence in a sad story | Because it is short | *It is an ordinary word for a plant, not a name | Because it is the name of a city
test: Why do the deer in Nara bow to visitors? | *They have learned to bob their heads for crackers | They are protected and cannot move | Because they are sacred and must bow to the Queen | They like to be butted by people
test: Which word is a proper name? | *Nara, the city in Japan | archives, the papers | deer, the animal | nara, the spiky melon
exam: Write one sentence about Nara Park using a capital letter for the proper name: | «Nara Park has tame Deer.» | *«Nara Park has tame deer.» | «nara Park has Tame deer.» | «nara park has tame deer.»
